e.** If an enemy bullet is close in its row, or an enemy sits on its back cell, it moves to an unblocked neighbouring row.\n3. **Hunt.** Otherwise it moves toward rows holding enemies or divers, weighting nearer rows more. Divers are collected simply by staying in their row while they drift into the submarine.\n4. **Never enter a blocked row.** A row is blocked if a hazard is within one column of the body.\n5. **Stay off rows 0 and 1.** It does not use rows 0 or 1, because a sticky \"up\" there could surface it with no diver, which ends the game.\n6. **Surface when needed.** When it has at least one diver and oxygen is below 60, it climbs to row 0. It then dives back down at once, waiting first if row 1 is dangerous.\n\n**Layer 1.** Each per-row unit is gated: the player cells in its row have weight 15 and the bias is about −30. So the unit equals tanh(local feature) when the player is in that row, and −1 otherwise. This makes the features relative to the player's row.\n- **H_r (rows 2–8, units 0–6).** Computes 0.5 + 0.15·(E + 2·O).\n  - E is enemies/bullets on the left minus those on the right.\n  - O is +1 when facing left and −1 when facing right, read from the back cell in the trail channel.\n  - The unit is only active when the body is exactly on columns 4 and 5.\n- **U_r (rows 2–8, units 7–13) and D_r (rows 2–7, units 14–19).** Each sums three things:\n  - attraction to targets above (U) or below (D);\n  - a −16 block for hazards next to the body in the adjacent row;\n  - a +8 threat for bullets in the current row, plus a \"stay\" penalty when a diver is in the current row.\n- **Global units:**\n  - S (unit 20): has a diver AND oxygen is below 60.\n  - S1 (unit 21): S while in row 1.\n  - R0 (unit 22): in row 0 with row 1 clear.\n  - R1 (unit 23): in row 1 with row 2 clear.\n  - Cx (unit 24): horizontal offset from the column-4/5 position.\n\n**Layer 2.**\n- **Units 0–6.** Thresholds on the H value split it into fire-left, turn-right, turn-left and fire-right zones.\n- **Units 7–11.** Read the U and D values as:\n  - an attraction level (7 for up, 10 for down);\n  - a threat step (8 for up, 11 for down);\n  - \"surface and the way up is free\" (9).\n- **Units 12–15.** Pass through S1, the two row-0/1 dive units, the centring unit and S.\n\n**Output logits.**\n- No-op: 0.\n- Fire: 2 at rest, 8 when an enemy is in line.\n- Turn (left or right): 5.\n- Up/down: about 4 for attraction, about 14 for a threat.\n- Surfacing: up to about 12–15.\n- Diving from row 0 or 1: about 6.7.\n\n```edits\n# ---------- H_r units 0..6 (rows 2..8) ----------\nW1[144,0]=15\nW1[150,0]=15\nW1[121:140:6,0]=0.15\nW1[157:176:6,0]=-0.15\nW1[154,0]=0.3\nW1[148,0]=-0.3\nW1[204,1]=15\nW1[210,1]=15\nW1[181:200:6,1]=0.15\nW1[217:236:6,1]=-0.15\nW1[214,1]=0.3\nW1[208,1]=-0.3\nW1[264,2]=15\nW1[270,2]=15\nW1[241:260:6,2]=0.15\nW1[277:296:6,2]=-0.15\nW1[274,2]=0.3\nW1[268,2]=-0.3\nW1[324,3]=15\nW1[330,3]=15\nW1[301:320:6,3]=0.15\nW1[337:356:6,3]=-0.15\nW1[334,3]=0.3\nW1[328,3]=-0.3\nW1[384,4]=15\nW1[390,4]=15\nW1[361:380:6,4]=0.15\nW1[397:416:6,4]=-0.15\nW1[394,4]=0.3\nW1[388,4]=-0.3\nW1[444,5]=15\nW1[450,5]=15\nW1[421:440:6,5]=0.15\nW1[457:476:6,5]=-0.15\nW1[454,5]=0.3\nW1[448,5]=-0.3\nW1[504,6]=15\nW1[510,6]=15\nW1[481:500:6,6]=0.15\nW1[517:536:6,6]=-0.15\nW1[514,6]=0.3\nW1[508,6]=-0.3\nb1[0:7]=-29.5\n# ---------- U_r units 7..13 (rows 2..8) ----------\nW1[120:180:6,7]=15\nW1[121:180:6,7]=[0.5,0.5,2.1,2.8,2.8,2.8,2.8,2.1,0.5,0.5]\nW1[122:180:6,7]=[-0.3,-0.3,-6,-8,0,0,-8,-6,-0.3,-0.3]\nW1[61:120:6,7]=[0,0,-1,-16,-16,-16,-16,-1,0,0]\nW1[180:240:6,8]=15\nW1[181:240:6,8]=[0.5,0.5,6,8,8,8,8,6,0.5,0.5]\nW1[182:240:6,8]=[-0.3,-0.3,-6,-8,0,0,-8,-6,-0.3,-0.3]\nW1[121:180:6,8]=[0,0,-1,-16,-16,-16,-16,-1,0,0]\nW1[122:180:6,8]=[1,1,2,1.6,1.6,1.6,1.6,2,1,1]\nW1[240:300:6,9]=15\nW1[241:300:6,9]=[0.5,0.5,6,8,8,8,8,6,0.5,0.5]\nW1[242:300:6,9]=[-0.3,-0.3,-6,-8,0,0,-8,-6,-0.3,-0.3]\nW1[181:240:6,9]=[0,0,-1,-16,-16,-16,-16,-1,0,0]\nW1[182:240:6,9]=[1,1,2,1.6,1.6,1.6,1.6,2,1,1